    "title": {
     "en": "A short story"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "Meena saw a candle burn and then saw salt crystals form from sea water.\n\"Are these the same kind of change?\" she asked."
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "explain",
    "type": "explanation",
    "provenance": "original",
    "keepEnglishTerms": [
     "chemical change",
     "physical change",
     "crystal"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "In a chemical change a new substance forms and it cannot be changed back easily. Rusting, burning, cooking an egg and curdling milk are chemical changes.\nIn a physical change no new substance forms. Melting ice, dissolving sugar and cutting paper are physical changes.\nCrystallisation is forming crystals from a solution when the water evaporates. It is a physical change."
    }
